insert into public.questions (id, test_id, prompt, options, position, passage) values
  ('0708e3b4-0efe-5573-b982-110cd695b6e3', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["yielding", "attenuated", "evolving", "entrenched"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The early twentieth-century modernist movement is often characterized in terms of revolutionary artists'' struggle against a static middle-class culture; by contending that the latter was itself ______, literary scholar Michael Levenson frames the conflict between the two not as a clash between dynamism and stagnation but instead as “a contest of novelties.”'),
  ('77ee2923-b5b4-5393-8df9-8c584078b1c4', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["an antithesis", "a replica", "a beneficiary", "an archetype"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Caracol, the famed Maya city located in the Central American nation of Belize, was likely ______ of achievements attained in the lesser-known polities of the Mirador Basin. As Morales-Aguilar et al. have shown, developments at those earlier Mirador sites (e.g., the eight astronomically aligned complexes at Balamunal) were a historical precondition for the sophistication exhibited by the architects of later cities.'),
  ('10194662-7701-5923-9dc3-0db22cb022b1', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'As used in the text, what does the word “breathes” most nearly mean?', '["Imparts", "Relinquishes", "Absorbs", "Surrenders"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The following text is adapted from the 1895 poem “Ojistoh” by Emily Pauline Johnson, a Kanien''kehá:ka (Mohawk) writer also known as Tekahionwake.

I am Ojistoh, I am she, the wife
Of him whose name <u>breathes</u> bravery and life
And courage to the tribe who calls him chief.
I am Ojistoh, his white star and he
Is land, and lake, and sky—and soul to me.'),
  ('628c11ba-917c-53ad-be47-77a238cc6b60', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["contrived", "repudiated", "amended", "foregrounded"]'::jsonb, 4, 'Artists affiliated with the Judson Dance Theater in the 1960s were dancers (including Elaine Summers) and creators from other fields (such as painter Alex Hay) interested in redefining the concept of dance. Rejecting formal techniques, the group ______ everyday movements: many pieces were built around ordinary actions, like sitting.'),
  ('b87d805b-0db7-5702-a06b-e529d44c0a4b', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?', '["efface", "misconstrue", "accentuate", "preempt"]'::jsonb, 5, 'Quantitative analysis of vast historical data sets and other tools of abstraction allow historians to examine broad phenomena, but such methods ______ the particularity of individual actors. By focusing on singular individuals and incidents in exhaustive detail, Laurel Thatcher Ulrich’s A Midwife’s Tale and other microhistories aim to show how broader phenomena were experienced at a human level.'),
  ('8345c783-7647-522d-9792-5ff607414b4b', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?', '["To evaluate the potential of two types of scientific instruments typically used for tracking GPP to also reliably measure SIF", "To explain why water availability and other factors influencing the relationship between GPP and SIF may compromise the reliability of GPP data obtained from flux towers", "To discuss a method for indirectly measuring GPP with remote-sensor technology that may compensate for a limitation associated with a standard method", "To identify the systemic errors associated with flux-tower estimates of GPP that prompted scientists to investigate alternate methods for gathering carbon flux data"]'::jsonb, 6, 'Scientists monitor ecosystem-wide plant health by tracking gross primary productivity (GPP)—the rate of carbon dioxide absorption by plants—through carbon flux data obtained on-site from flux towers. But as flux towers aren’t evenly distributed globally, alternate proxies for GPP obtained remotely from satellite sensors, including solar-induced chlorophyll fluorescence (SIF) emitted by plants during photosynthesis, are being investigated. The GPP-SIF relationship, which is mediated by water availability and other factors, isn’t completely understood, but studies suggest that SIF typically correlates well with flux-tower data.'),
  ('deb187f2-1891-5127-ba05-844240726c79', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?', '["It suggests that a hypothesis discussed later in the text regarding a potential visual cue that hummingbirds rely on to increase their foraging efficiency has little support from the broader scientific community.", "It acknowledges research findings, which weren’t replicated by the study discussed later in the text, positing a relationship between floral traits that potentially underlies hummingbird foraging decisions.", "It attributes the inconclusive findings reported in the text regarding the influence of a particular floral trait on interactions between hummingbirds and plants to differences in study sites.", "It summarizes contradictory study findings concerning a floral trait that influences hummingbird foraging patterns, which the study mentioned later in the text aimed to resolve."]'::jsonb, 7, 'Visiting flowers that produce high volumes of nectar allows hummingbirds, including fiery-throated hummingbirds, to maximize their foraging efficiency. But nectar can’t be seen from outside the flower and <u>while some studies have suggested that petal length may indicate nectar volume</u>, Maria A. Maglianesi and team found no such association among hummingbird-visited plants at Villa Mills Experimental Biological Station and other sites in Costa Rica. The researchers hypothesize that by driving hummingbirds to visit more plants in search of high-reward flowers, plants'' lack of reliable signaling may increase chances of pollination.'),
  ('c22b71fc-e26a-5270-b13d-e6e9a9aaceb7', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice best states the main idea of the text?', '["Although Malta, Sardinia, and Sicily all show evidence of lithic industry in the sixth and seventh millennia BCE, the characteristics of the stone tools in each location suggest three distinct levels of technological sophistication.", "While not definitive evidence, the materials and methods used in the production of Maltese stone tools in the sixth and seventh millennia BCE are strongly suggestive of the exchange of lithic technology between Malta, Sardinia, and Sicily.", "The characteristics of Maltese stone tools from the sixth and seventh millennia BCE are indicative of a level of lithic technological development that, while not uniquely low, was less advanced than that observed nearby in Sicily.", "Maltese stone tools from the sixth and seventh millennia BCE are notable for their relative simplicity and their similarity with stone tools produced in Sicily."]'::jsonb, 8, 'Maltese lithic (stone implement) assemblages from the sixth and seventh millennia BCE exhibit notable characteristics. Nearly all implements were fashioned from limestone—mostly from beach cobbles—rather than superior chert or obsidian, and the assemblages predominantly comprise flakes produced through direct percussion, with negligible representation of cores, blades, or retouched tools. The fairly rudimentary nature of Malta’s lithic industry parallels contemporaneous Sardinian technologies rather than the sophisticated geometric microlith traditions documented in neighboring Sicily.'),
  ('d374bea1-9820-51c8-9e74-07b332c4b782', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Based on the text, how did Marshall’s Brown v. Board of Education case most likely influence the US legal system’s approach to civil rights?', '["It promoted the idea that legal action is the most efficient way to create social change.", "It established that the courts could be used as a tool for significant social change.", "It led courts to focus more on clarifying existing civil rights laws than on making modifications to them.", "It inadvertently resulted in the courts taking a more cautious, incremental approach to advancing subsequent civil rights cases."]'::jsonb, 9, 'Thurgood Marshall saw litigation as a means to enact social reforms and advance equal justice for US citizens. He cited the law’s “capacity to initiate change and its flexibility to accept and mold change” as vital, breaking with the historical tradition of wielding the courts primarily to clarify or modify existing laws. This vision was realized in Marshall’s successful arguing of the 1954 Brown v. Board of Education case before the US Supreme Court, as the court’s decision to overturn the long-standing “separate but equal” doctrine revolutionized how the legal system regarded civil rights.'),
  ('2d188995-b824-5ab5-a45f-b0242ed8d445', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the assertion?', '["the rate of damage to the pears was approximately 7% in the area with the repeller attached to a neural network and approximately 13% in the area where no repeller was used.", "the greatest rate of damage to the pears occurred in the area of the orchard where no repeller was used.", "the lowest rate of damage occurred in the area of the orchard where the repeller was not attached to a neural network.", "the rate of damage to the pears was approximately 6% in the area with the repeller attached to a neural network and approximately 7% in the area with the repeller not attached to a neural network."]'::jsonb, 10, '![figure](/q/may26/001.webp)

Finches and other pest birds can cause damage to grapes and other fruits grown on farms by pecking at them and spoiling them. Aware of some practical limitations of predator decoys and other common deterrents, Qing Chen et al. investigated the utility of an inexpensive, easily installed sonic bird repeller in a pear orchard. In one area the repeller emitted a sound continuously, while in another it emitted a sound only when triggered by a webcam linked to a neural network trained to recognize a pest bird’s presence. (A third area without a repeller was used as a control condition.) Chen et al. concluded that an intermittently active sonic repellent is more effective than one that is constantly active, as evidenced by the fact that ______'),
  ('4287abbb-e8d2-531e-81f4-62f74824bde6', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the example?', '["mute swan, which has an average mass of 11.9 kg.", "Andean condor, which has an average mass below 10 kg.", "Somali ostrich, which has a higher average mass than the dwarf cassowary.", "Somali ostrich, which has an average mass of 90.0 kg."]'::jsonb, 11, '**Bird Species by Average Mass**

| Common name | Average mass (kg) | Capable of flight? |
| Dwarf cassowary | 19.7 | No |
| Somali ostrich | 90.0 | No |
| Mute swan | 11.9 | Yes |
| Andean condor | 11.3 | Yes |

Most bird species that are capable of flight weigh less than a kilogram (kg), which is not surprising considering the burden that extra body weight puts on a flying animal. But not all flying birds are so light, as we can see most clearly in the example of the ______'),
  ('c1263ae6-70d9-5b1d-b97c-60a86da68899', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to support the researchers''
recommendation?', '["The 10% SSA mixture’s compressive strength was greater than that of the control mixture on day 7, but by day 28 the 10% SSA mixture’s compressive strength had decreased while that of the control mixture had increased.", "The compressive strength of the 10% SSA mixture remained nearly the same from day 7 to day 28, while that of the 20% and 40% SSA mixtures changed substantially.", "The 10% SSA mixture’s compressive strength was greater than or approximately equal to that of the control mixture on day 7 and on day 28, but on both days the 20% and 40% SSA mixtures had less compressive strength than the control mixture did.", "The compressive strength of the 10% SSA mixture never surpassed the compressive strength measured for the control mixture on day 28."]'::jsonb, 12, '![figure](/q/may26/002.webp)

Mollusk shells are mainly composed of calcium carbonate, a chemical compound used in mortar and other construction materials. A research team led by Ariane da Silva Cardoso investigated pulverizing discarded Sururu mussel shells to create a substitute for fine aggregates (such as sand) in mortar mixtures. The team prepared mixtures with Sururu shell aggregate (SSA) replacing varying percentages of sand and then tested the mortars'' compressive strength on days 7 and 28 of curing. Based on their findings, the team recommended SSA substitution in relatively small proportions to avoid compromising strength.'),
  ('2250b9b4-ff90-5498-979a-d0fb97a0e7b0', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the assertion?', '["those that filed Form 4720 because they did not meet the minimum charitable distribution requirement paid, on average, higher penalties than those organizations that filed Form 990 but also filed Form 4720 for the same reason.", "those that filed Form 4720 because they engaged in self-dealing paid, on average, lower penalties than those that filed Form 4720 because they did not meet the minimum charitable distribution requirement.", "those that filed Form 4720 because they engaged in self-dealing and those that filed Form 4720 because of their taxable expenditures collectively paid a smaller portion of the total penalty than those that filed Form 4720 because they did not meet the minimum charitable distribution requirement.", "more filed Form 4720 because they failed to meet the minimum charitable distribution requirement than did so in the following year."]'::jsonb, 13, '![figure](/q/may26/003.webp)

While US public charities, like Habitat for Humanity International, must file Form 990 yearly with the IRS, private foundations, such as Lilly Endowment Inc., must file a different form, 990-PF. In addition, foundations that engage in certain prohibited activities must also file Form 4720 and pay a penalty tax on the money involved. Prohibited activities for private foundations include “self-dealing” (conducting activities that benefit foundation insiders), making taxable expenditures such as grants to noncharitable entities, and failing to cross a required threshold in making charitable distributions from income. Out of the organizations that filed Form 990-PF in the year 2005, ______'),
  ('bb7c283d-30b1-502b-8252-12e83f6d70d3', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which finding, if true, would most directly challenge the assertion about the Bantu expansion presented in the text?', '["Lexical reconstructions indicate that the earliest Bantu speakers'' words for yams, starchy tubers that are today an agricultural staple throughout sub-Saharan Africa, were inherited from languages predating the arrival of Bantu ancestral groups in their homeland.", "Among the earliest archaeobotanical evidence of plant farming in East Africa, which Bantu-speaking peoples may have reached as early as 3,500 ya, are traces of cowpea (Vigna unguiculata), a legume crop believed to have originated in West Africa, which were discovered in the Kakapel Rockshelter in present-day Kenya.", "The earliest unambiguous archaeobotanical evidence of plant cultivation and domestication in West-Central Africa consists of pearl millet (Pennisetum glaucum) found in three sites in present-day Cameroon dated to around 2,200-2,350 ya and in one site in the present-day Democratic Republic of the Congo dated to around 2,200 ya.", "Reconstructed vocabulary from Proto-Bantu, the ancestral language from which all later Bantu languages descended, contains terms for some wild plant species that early Bantu speakers actively managed and cultivated but that were never fully domesticated into true crop plants."]'::jsonb, 14, 'The Bantu expansion refers to the gradual dispersal of Bantu-speaking peoples (which today include, among other groups, the Tutsi in Rwanda and the Zulu in South Africa) and their languages from an ancestral homeland in West-Central Africa across much of sub-Saharan Africa over approximately 3,500 years, starting about 4,000-5,000 years ago (ya). Citing the discovery of pounding equipment dating as far back as 5,000 ya consistent with processing of plant foods, some researchers have asserted that the Bantu expansion can be explained by the farming/language dispersal hypothesis. This hypothesis proposes that the dispersal of many of the world’s large language families—for instance, Indo-European —was driven primarily by the adoption of agriculture.'),
  ('d95f9025-88a0-5a87-8738-bbab75bf8bc6', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice most logically completes the text?', '["far fewer gold objects dating to earlier than 1500 BCE have been recovered from sites in the Caucasus than have been recovered from comparably old sites outside the region.", "there is a positive relationship between the number of gold objects found at Caucasus sites and the sites'' respective distances from nearby sources of gold, such as gold ore deposits.", "the proportion of gold objects to other types of objects recovered is significantly higher at Kazbegi than at Horom despite the two sites'' close proximity.", "a much larger number of Caucasus sites dating from after 1500 BCE are represented in the dataset than sites dating from before 1500 BCE are."]'::jsonb, 15, 'Episodes in which technologies fall into disuse after a period of adoption, as occurred with the disappearance of Roman concrete as a construction material around 500 CE, are informative for understanding the factors shaping technological development in ancient societies. However, it can be unclear whether an absence of artifacts signifies a cultural shift or is merely an effect of gaps in the archaeological record. A dataset of gold objects, including pendants and vessels, recovered from Bronze and Iron Age sites at Kazbegi, Horom, and other places in the Caucasus reveals a steep drop in the total number of gold artifacts beginning around 1500 BCE in some locations. That this drop represents a genuine instance of cultural change is likely, given that ______'),
  ('f8dbd866-6ef9-5567-8685-d9fca77c3f89', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["will constitute", "had constituted", "constitute", "constituted"]'::jsonb, 16, 'The ancient city of Caral stretches across 150 acres of the Supe Valley in Peru. When archaeologists first surveyed the site in the early 1900s, they mistook its six massive earth-and-rock pyramids for natural formations; now, these monumental structures ______ some of the earliest evidence of urban civilization in the Americas, reshaping how scholars understand the origins of complex societies.'),
  ('d8364a06-8627-509f-988d-e84f8649c298', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["being", "was", "were", "are"]'::jsonb, 17, 'The Nimatron was an early digital computer designed to play a mathematical game against visitors to the 1939-1940 New York World’s Fair. Though capable of making game moves in milliseconds, this one-ton machine—built by Westinghouse Electric Corporation engineers to demonstrate how electrical relays could respond to players'' choices according to predetermined mathematical patterns—______ programmed with time delays to give the impression of deliberative thinking.'),
  ('608bb309-5132-54ef-8316-2565d98fd134', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["“clothing”),", "clothing”)—", "“clothing”)", "“clothing”);"]'::jsonb, 18, 'In English metrical poetry, disyllabic words that consist of one unstressed syllable followed by one stressed syllable, like “morale,” are called iambs, whereas disyllabic words in which the unstressed syllable follows the stressed one (such as ______ are classified as trochees.'),
  ('edda7095-1f30-51ca-afd8-ec60c2484c31', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["considering", "were considering", "had considered", "considered"]'::jsonb, 19, 'The economies of “The Four Asian Tigers”—Hong Kong, Singapore, South Korea, and Taiwan—saw tremendous growth in the late 20th century. Scholars ______ cultural explanations for this phenomenon, likely recalling Weber’s association of capitalism with religion in Reformation-era northern Europe, posited that Confucianism’s emphasis on hard work, discipline, education, and respect for authority laid the groundwork for the Tigers'' economic success.'),
  ('8791d1c3-7f92-58b0-9e97-55e603c7c3d8', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["poets challenging", "poets. Challenging", "poets, challenging", "poets-challenging"]'::jsonb, 20, 'Although popular during her lifetime, the writer Helen Maria Williams (1759-1827) doesn’t often feature in twentieth-century studies of British Romantic poetry—a body of scholarship predominantly focused on the era’s six major male ______ the exclusivity of the traditional Romantic canon, Lia Guerra and other contemporary literary critics have published new research on Williams’s poetry and life, thereby repositioning Williams as an important Romantic writer.'),
  ('85843014-6d05-5515-b2f3-db8b82659cd2', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?', '["Chesnutt and Dunbars''", "Chesnutts and Dunbars''", "Chesnutt and Dunbar''s", "Chesnutt’s and Dunbar''s"]'::jsonb, 21, 'The Marrow of Tradition, a 1901 novel by Charles Chesnutt, has been lauded as “probably the most astute political-historical novel of its day,” while The Sport of the Gods, a 1902 novel by Paul Laurence Dunbar, was recently praised for “expos[ing] the disjuncture between law and justice” in the US at the time. ______ novels are just two of several by Black authors from the period to have garnered such acclaim.'),
  ('122b27f2-346d-5dfe-8c32-af77b44e31a8', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["To determine where they went wrong,", "In light of this limitation,", "To correct this misconception,", "Addressing the flaws in their hypothesis,"]'::jsonb, 22, 'Researchers have long been aware that pistol shrimp use a specialized claw to create bubbles that stun their prey, but understanding of the phenomenon has been limited by researchers'' inability to accurately measure the tiny, rapid movements of the shrimp. ______ scientists have turned to computer simulations to re-create the claw’s closing motion, allowing them to track the pressure, speed, and density of water throughout the bubble formation.'),
  ('996b301a-b74f-51d9-9fd6-b693d6d0dd3a', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["Additionally,", "Likewise,", "Consequently,", "Conversely,"]'::jsonb, 23, 'A recent study found that groups of Paratrechina longicornis ants solved a geometric puzzle more efficiently than human groups. While humans performed well as individuals because of strategic thinking, working in teams did not enhance humans'' problem-solving efficiency. ______ as part of a closely connected colony, the ants effectively used shared memory and coordination, collectively solving a problem that no ant could have solved alone.'),
  ('ea36ee65-ff52-5ee7-badf-e4145f5e2725', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?', '["The book’s title alludes to an example of this social shift:", "Some critics have presented evidence that the book may overstate the data’s significance:", "This argument, though valid, may overlook other forms of group participation:", "According to Putnam, this decline has broader social implications:"]'::jsonb, 24, 'In his 2000 book Bowling Alone, sociologist Robert Putnam argues that the erosion of social capital in the United States can be traced to the waning popularity of a variety of civic organizations, such as scouting groups, labor unions, and sports clubs. ______ between 1980 and 1993, though the number of bowlers in the country increased by 10 percent, the number of bowlers participating in a league decreased by 40 percent.'),
  ('a0459046-0a38-5750-b2f9-c8ac594c5faa', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'Which choice most effectively uses information from the given sentences to introduce Mexia to a new audience?', '["Between 1917 and 1938, Ynes Mexia collected samples of the plants Erigeron humilis and Mikania confertissima, among others.", "Among the many botanical samples Ynes Mexia collected in the United States in 1928 was Erigeron humilis of the Asteraceae family.", "Many of the botanical samples collected by Ynes Mexia, such as Erigeron humilis and Mikania confertissima, can now be viewed on the C.V. Starr Virtual Herbarium.", "Botanist Ynes Mexia is known for collecting over 150,000 botanical samples throughout the Americas between 1917 and 1938."]'::jsonb, 25, 'Ynes Mexia was a Mexican American botanist.
Between 1917 and 1938, she collected over 150,000 botanical samples throughout the Americas. She collected a sample of Erigeron humilis in Alaska, the United States, in 1928.
She collected a sample of Mikania confertissima in Minas Gerais, Brazil, in 1930.
Erigeron humilis and Mikania confertissima are part of the Asteraceae family.
These specimens can now be viewed online at the C.V. Starr Virtual Herbarium.'),
  ('306cfd8e-2423-5664-8a4d-bd404c92b648', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'The student wants to contrast how shear affects hair gel and oobleck. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["Hair gel becomes thinner when squeezed, while oobleck becomes thicker.", "Though the viscosities of both oobleck and hair gel change under shear, oobleck’s typical resting viscosity (5-100 cP) is lower than that of hair gel (3,000-30,000 cP).", "Oobleck has a much lower resting viscosity than hair gel but becomes thicker under shear.", "Hair gel is non-Newtonian, meaning its viscosity decreases under shear; oobleck, by contrast, increases in viscosity."]'::jsonb, 26, 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:

The typical resting viscosity of oobleck (cornstarch mixed with water) is 5-100 centipoise (cP). Oobleck increases in viscosity (becomes thicker) when squeezed.
The typical resting viscosity of hair gel is 3,000-30,000 (cP).
Hair gel decreases in viscosity (becomes thinner) when squeezed.
A fluid is Newtonian if its viscosity remains stable under shear (mechanical force such as being squeezed or stirred).
A fluid is non-Newtonian if its viscosity changes under shear.'),
  ('d483aeeb-6970-5771-a97b-56e594adfba5', 'e9ab7ecf-4f0e-5e54-a487-f2960da99315', 'The student wants to emphasize a difference between Barilla’s and Kasko’s uses of FDM printing technology. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?', '["Barilla and Kasko have developed different uses for FDM printing, a 3D printing technology also known as material extrusion.", "Barilla uses FDM printing to build layers of pasta dough into unique shapes, whereas Kasko uses FDM printing to build layers of uniquely shaped cakes.", "While both Barilla and Kasko use FDM printers to create uniquely shaped 3D objects, Barilla is using the technology to produce food and Kasko isn’t.", "FDM printing technology has many uses, from creating uniquely shaped pasta from semolina and water dough to constructing cake molds from silicone."]'::jsonb, 27, 'While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:

Fused deposition modeling (FDM) is one type of 3D printing technology.
FDM is also called material extrusion.
FDM printers eject a modeling medium through a heated nozzle to build an object layer by layer. Italian company Barilla uses FDM printers that extrude layers of semolina and water dough to create unique shapes of pasta.
Ukrainian entrepreneur Dinara Kasko uses an FDM printer that extrudes layers of silicone to create uniquely shaped molds for baking cakes.')
on conflict (id) do update set test_id = excluded.test_id, prompt = excluded.prompt, options = excluded.options,
  position = excluded.position, passage = excluded.passage;
insert into public.question_keys (question_id, correct_index, correct_answers, explanation) values
  ('0708e3b4-0efe-5573-b982-110cd695b6e3', 2, null, 'If middle-class culture was itself changing, the conflict is "a contest of novelties": it was "evolving."'),
  ('77ee2923-b5b4-5393-8df9-8c584078b1c4', 2, null, 'Mirador developments were a precondition for Caracol''s sophistication, so Caracol benefited from them.'),
  ('10194662-7701-5923-9dc3-0db22cb022b1', 0, null, 'His name gives bravery and life to the tribe: "imparts."'),
  ('628c11ba-917c-53ad-be47-77a238cc6b60', 3, null, 'Pieces were built around ordinary actions, so the group put everyday movement front and center.'),
  ('b87d805b-0db7-5702-a06b-e529d44c0a4b', 0, null, 'Broad abstraction erases individual detail, which microhistories try to restore: "efface."'),
  ('8345c783-7647-522d-9792-5ff607414b4b', 2, null, 'SIF from satellites may stand in for GPP where flux towers are scarce.'),
  ('deb187f2-1891-5127-ba05-844240726c79', 1, null, 'It cites earlier findings linking petal length and nectar, which Maglianesi''s study did not find.'),
  ('c22b71fc-e26a-5270-b13d-e6e9a9aaceb7', 2, null, 'Maltese tools were simple like Sardinia''s and less advanced than Sicily''s microliths.'),
  ('d374bea1-9820-51c8-9e74-07b332c4b782', 1, null, 'Brown v. Board showed litigation could drive major social change, as Marshall envisioned.'),
  ('2d188995-b824-5ab5-a45f-b0242ed8d445', 3, null, 'The webcam-triggered repeller had about 6% damage vs about 7% for the continuous one.'),
  ('4287abbb-e8d2-531e-81f4-62f74824bde6', 0, null, 'The mute swan flies yet averages 11.9 kg, far above 1 kg.'),
  ('c1263ae6-70d9-5b1d-b97c-60a86da68899', 2, null, '10% SSA matched or beat the control on both days, while 20% and 40% were weaker.'),
  ('2250b9b4-ff90-5498-979a-d0fb97a0e7b0', 2, null, 'Self-dealing (about 40%) and taxable expenditures (about 4%) together are below undistributed income''s roughly 55% of penalties.'),
  ('bb7c283d-30b1-502b-8252-12e83f6d70d3', 2, null, 'If cultivation in the homeland appears only about 2,200 years ago, farming can''t explain an expansion that began 4,000-5,000 years ago.'),
  ('d95f9025-88a0-5a87-8738-bbab75bf8bc6', 3, null, 'More sites after 1500 BCE are in the data, so fewer gold objects isn''t a sampling gap.'),
  ('f8dbd866-6ef9-5567-8685-d9fca77c3f89', 2, null, 'A present, ongoing fact ("now"): "constitute."'),
  ('d8364a06-8627-509f-988d-e84f8649c298', 1, null, 'The singular subject "machine" takes "was."'),
  ('608bb309-5132-54ef-8316-2565d98fd134', 2, null, 'The closing quote and parenthesis are followed directly by the verb "are," with no comma.'),
  ('edda7095-1f30-51ca-afd8-ec60c2484c31', 0, null, '"Scholars considering..." is the subject phrase; "posited" is the main verb.'),
  ('8791d1c3-7f92-58b0-9e97-55e603c7c3d8', 1, null, 'Two complete sentences: a period after "poets."'),
  ('85843014-6d05-5515-b2f3-db8b82659cd2', 3, null, 'Two separate novels, each owned separately: "Chesnutt''s and Dunbar''s."'),
  ('122b27f2-346d-5dfe-8c32-af77b44e31a8', 1, null, 'Because measurements were limited, scientists used simulations: "In light of this limitation."'),
  ('996b301a-b74f-51d9-9fd6-b693d6d0dd3a', 3, null, 'The ants'' success in groups contrasts with the humans: "Conversely."'),
  ('ea36ee65-ff52-5ee7-badf-e4145f5e2725', 0, null, 'The bowling data illustrate the decline and explain the book''s title.'),
  ('a0459046-0a38-5750-b2f9-c8ac594c5faa', 3, null, 'It introduces who Mexia was and her main achievement.'),
  ('306cfd8e-2423-5664-8a4d-bd404c92b648', 0, null, 'It contrasts the effect of squeezing: gel thins, oobleck thickens.'),
  ('d483aeeb-6970-5771-a97b-56e594adfba5', 2, null, 'It highlights the difference: Barilla makes food, Kasko makes molds (not food).')
